\viewkind4\uc1\pard\tx3780\tx3960\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Light of the lonely pilgrim's heart,
\par Star of the coming day,
\par Arise, and with Thy morning beams
\par Chase all our griefs away.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Come, blessed Lord, bid every shore
\par And answering island sing 
\par The praises of Thy royal name,
\par And own Thee as their King.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. Bid the whole earth, responsive now
\par To the bright world above,
\par Break forth in rapturous strains of joy
\par In memory of Thy love.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. Jesus, Thy fair creation groans-
\par The air, the earth, the sea-
\par In unison with all our hearts,
\par And calls aloud for Thee.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. Thine was the Cross, with all its fruits
\par Of grace and peace divine ;
\par Be Thine the crown of glory now,
\par The palm of victory Thine.\tab 
\par                                  Amen.\i 
\par \pard\i0\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\f2 
\par }

